<</P 3305 0 R/S/Diagram/Alt(The EXISTS and UNIQUE Functions in SQL\rEXISTS and UNIQUE are Boolean functions that return TRUE or FALSE; hence, they can be used in a WHERE clause condition. \rThe EXISTS function in SQL is used to check whether the result of a nested query is empty \(contains no tuples\) or not.\rThe result of EXISTS is a Boolean value TRUE if the nested query result contains at least one tuple, or FALSE if the nested query result contains no tuples.\r\(Vertical Bullet List\)) /Type/StructElem/K[ 1] /Pg 144 0 R/A 3310 0 R>>
